BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:a69772a5e51bb71f@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192328Z
DTSTART:20260729T130000Z
DTEND:20260729T150000Z
SUMMARY:The Democracy to Come-Ambedkar\, Fanon\, and the Time of Counter-
 Revolution
LOCATION:Conference Room I\, IIC main\, India International Centre\, 40 M
 ax Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/democracy-come-ambedkar-fanon-and-time
 -counter-revolution
DESCRIPTION:The Democracy to Come\nAmbedkar\, Fanon\, and the Time of Cou
 nter-Revolution\nSpeaker: Dr Aishwary Kumar\, Professor of History of Pol
 itical Thought and Institutions\, and Director of The Democracy Institute
  at Cal Poly Pomona\, Chair\, The GIFT Project and the American Instituti
 ons Common Core\nChair: Dr Mujibur Rehman\, faculty\, Jamia Millia Centra
 l University\, New Delhi\nIntroductory Remarks: Dr Usha Munshi\, Chief Li
 brarian\, IIC\nThe concept of “counter-revolution” occupies a galvani
 zing place in B. R. Ambedkar’s political thought and moral psychology. 
 Unlike nationalists of his time\, Ambedkar rarely speaks of extreme viole
 nce and exploitation as a function simply of modern colonial bondage. Ins
 tead\, for him\, “inequality” is force\, a spectrum of compulsions\, 
 a desire even. Which is why its cruelty can be grasped only as a counter-
 revolutionary form that alters our very relationship to time and authorit
 y. Counter-revolution as a neo-democratic form: this singular insight—w
 hat I call "the caste contract"—puts Ambedkar in an exemplary constella
 tion of abolitionist thinkers on human freedom and moral judgment who ret
 urn to us today with a dark urgency.\n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/de
 mocracy-come-ambedkar-fanon-and-time-counter-revolution
CATEGORIES:talk\,sociology
END:VEVENT
