BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:08a76e09e95f1990@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192328Z
DTSTART:20260802T133000Z
DTEND:20260802T153000Z
SUMMARY:She Walked Anyway
LOCATION:Casuarina\, India Habitat Centre\, Lodhi Road\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://indiahabitat.org/Events_details/1332
DESCRIPTION:Book Launch & Discussion . She Walked Anyway by Dr. Sazina Kh
 an . A collection of poems and a lyrical meditation on quiet courage\, in
 ner reclamation\, and the profound strength of moving forward without per
 mission or validation. Through evocative poems such as Unannounced Becomi
 ng\, Permissionless\, Grace\, Unrequested\, The Yes I Gave Myself\, and B
 ecoming Without Allowance \, this collection traces the inner evolution o
 f a woman who chooses motion over hesitation and self-trust over approval
 . Publisher: White Falcon . The author will be in conversation on Walking
  Through Storms: Women\, Memory and the Making of the Inner Self with Oro
 on Das \, actor\, theatre artist and Dr. Gilles Chuyen \, director\, chor
 eographer\, actor. Moderator: Meera Khanna \, writer\, poet\, Trustee & P
 resident\, The Guild for Service. Chief Guest: Prof. (Dr.) K. G. Suresh \
 , Director\, India Habitat Centre.\n\nhttps://indiahabitat.org/Events_det
 ails/1332
CATEGORIES:talk\,literature
END:VEVENT
