UID:d63b893a4a2d8691@delhi-events
DTSTAMP:20260728T192328Z
DTSTART:20260803T130000Z
DTEND:20260803T150000Z
SUMMARY:Cleaning Transport – Tackling Vehicular Emissions and the Futur
 e of Mobility Uniting Science\, Health\, Policy & People
LOCATION:Lecture Room II\, IIC Annexe\, India International Centre\, 40 M
 ax Mueller Marg\, Lodhi Gardens\, New Delhi 110003
URL:https://iicdelhi.in/programmes/cleaning-transport-tackling-vehicular-
 emissions-and-future-mobility-uniting-science
DESCRIPTION:Cleaning Transport – Tackling Vehicular Emissions and the F
 uture of Mobility\nUniting Science\, Health\, Policy & People\nModerator:
  Sarika Panda\, Co-founder\, Raahgiri Foundation and Director\, Nagarro\n
 Discussants: Dr. Virinder Sharma\, Member (Technical)\, CAQM\; Niharika R
 ai\, Secretary-cum-Commissioner\, Transport Dpt\, Govt of NCT of Delhi\; 
 Mahmood Ahmed\, Additional Secretary (Transport)\, Ministry of Road Trans
 port and Highways\; J. Ganesan\, Chairman\, Haryana State Pollution Contr
 ol Board\; Amit Bhatt\, India Managing Director\, International Council o
 n Clean Transportation\; Trupti Deshpande\, Energiva Ventures\nTransition
 ing to clean urban mobility yields profound benefits—ranging from impro
 ved air quality and reduced greenhouse gas emissions to quieter and more 
 livable cities. This session will explore how to accelerate the shift tow
 ard zero-emission transport by scaling up electric vehicle ecosystems\, m
 odernizing public transit networks\, and enforcing stringent emission reg
 ulations.\nThis is the fourth discussion in the series of dialogues under
  the umbrella of ‘Uniting Science\, Health\, Policy & People’\n(Colla
 boration: Commission for Air Quality Management (CAQM) and Raahgiri Found
 ation)\n\nhttps://iicdelhi.in/programmes/cleaning-transport-tackling-vehi
 cular-emissions-and-future-mobility-uniting-science
CATEGORIES:talk\,science\,sociology
END:VEVENT
